 people  a married socialite from New Hampshire  and an ex-con from New Mexico who have  shared an inexplicable mental connection  since childhood that neither understands  as the connection deepens they realize  they aren't going crazy because there is  actually another person inside their  heads but while they know they're sane  the rest of the world isn't so sure the  way back based on a memoir by a former  Polish prisoner of war the way back  tells the incredible story of a group of  POWs who escaped from a Siberian gulag  and walk over four thousand miles  crossing deserts and even the Himalayas  in an epic quest to find freedom this  change is serving  there's nowhere to hide its also  features amazing cinematography as well  as a stellar cast including Colin  Farrell and Oscar nominees Edie Harris  and Saoirse Ronan old boy while an  American version of old boy directed by  Spike Lee was released in 2013 the  original south korean movie is far  superior and it's on Netflix for your  viewing pleasure based on a Japanese  manga old boy is a thrilling neo-noir  mystery centred on the story of a man  who was abducted and held for 15 years  in a prison cell with no knowledge of  who his captors are or why they are  keeping him there learn to walk more Abu  anga coochie mah nà no luck then he  finds himself suddenly released and  given the chance to get revenge on his  captors if he can find them in a mere  five days and then well we can't say  anything else about spoiling the many  shocks on surprises kung fury funded  entirely by Kickstarter kung fury  debuted at the Cannes Film Festival  before being released free of charge on  YouTube where it gained such a cult  following that it's secured  international distribution on Netflix as  crazy as that story is though it pales  in comparison to the utterly insane 80s  action parody mashup that installs on  your screen with everything from  time-traveling demigods to dinosaur cops  - kung fu Hitler kung fury delivers 